{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932599-battles-of-influence-newspapers-police-investigations-etc","id":932599,"title":"Battles of Influence? NewsPapers, Police Investigations, Etc","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-16T12:48:02-07:00","id":932599,"title":"Battles of Influence? NewsPapers, Police Investigations, Etc","content":"A not infrequent occurence in many World of Darkness games may be tugs of war on influence.<br /> <br /> How to make sure a News story is printed, is squeelched, or is slanted to your liking<br /> <br /> How to influence school curricula.<br /> <br /> Or The police investigation you decide is problematic.<br /> <br /> Especialy bad for WTA chars who dont use the influence background but might still have substantial control on a newspaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T09:55:10-07:00","id":933461,"title":"","content":"Is there a question here?<br /> <br /> And just because Influence isn't normally a background in Werewolf (or any other game) doesn't mean it can't be ported over just fine.<br /> Personally, I use the old MET influence backgrounds (street, university, police etc.) and make them available in any game I run. If players don't want them, they don't take them and nothing is lost. But they can add a lot to fleshing out a characters background if players want to go that route.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T10:15:22-07:00","id":933469,"title":"","content":"How to handle mechanicly the tug of war between say a kinfolk or ghoul working in the local newspaper trying to bury a story, and a Truth seeking Zealout? or worse, a Ferectoi trying to slant things horribly.<br /> <br /> Since both parties try to destroy things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T10:17:56-07:00","id":933471,"title":"","content":"Well how do you think a news paper works? <br /> In the flow chart to get something printed anyone with the title &quot;editor&quot; can squash a story or get it buried so far off the front page no one will probably read it. <br /> <br /> Also anyone who owns the news paper can have a strong say in what sorts of news gets printed. <br /> <br /> Now this may have been the case 20 years ago but in today's blog o sphere if a reporter gets told by his editor to squash a story there is nothing preventing them from just posting it on an alt news site.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":".  Little rude, but really this is some common sense stuff. 07-18-2016, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T10:26:56-07:00","id":933476,"title":"","content":"So yea, for this sort of thing I default to using the system in <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1533/The-Masquerade-2nd-Edition?cPath=1_16&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">The Masquerade</a>. I have the book on hand and it works well enough. I'm not sure if later Larp books improved this system at all since I don't have any of those books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T11:08:11-07:00","id":933491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932599-battles-of-influence-newspapers-police-investigations-etc?p=933476#post933476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yea, for this sort of thing I default to using the system in <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1533/The-Masquerade-2nd-Edition?cPath=1_16&amp;it=1&quot;]The</a> Masquerade[/URL]. I have the book on hand and it works well enough. I'm not sure if later Larp books improved this system at all since I don't have any of those books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The larp system did a great job of breaking it down level wise of what you can or can not do across the various spheres of influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T17:00:39-07:00","id":937834,"title":"","content":"The Internet is full of crazy stories. I still occasionally come across people claiming that Presidents Bush and Obama are part of conspiracy to run death camps against Christians. If you want to discredit an Internet story about vampires, just have your ghoul hackers link it to stories like that one. In a few days, the reporter's bylines will not even be printed on toilet paper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T10:39:13-07:00","id":938199,"title":"","content":"I have a long-running <i>Mage </i>game that takes place in L.A. (name of the chronicle is <i>Wonder Why They Call You Witch</i>), and as the characters got more powerful, they wanted new and measurable ways to gauge and flex their influence. Being a group that tends towards preferring more crunch rather than less, I developed the following system of &quot;Areas of Influence&quot; which basically create backgrounds, each of which has five levels (or dots) that may purchased and provide various and sundry capabilities. There are Police Ties, Government and Municipal Services (which my players just call &quot;Political Ties&quot;), and Media Ties. This is a link to that PDF document: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/vzlu64qe3o8356h/Areas%20of%20Influence.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/vzlu64qe3o...uence.pdf?dl=0</a><br /> <br /> Mind you I tailored lots of it to Los Angeles' own county and municipal organization--other municipalities organized differently (which depends heavily on whether that state's constitution has a strong &quot;home rule&quot; provision for counties and cities) won't necessarily match up perfectly to all the stuff I have, but I suspect it would be easily adapted. If the game goes long enough, I will probably develop a level something for Federal government ties, though that's a trickier cat to skin given the depth of that bureaucracy (so it would probably end up being applicable to only a given Federal district).<br /> <br /> Please don't hesitate to throw me feedback. The system has been working well for my group thus far, but I don't think it's been really put through its paces yet, so I guess the ultimate determination over whether it's any good is still to come.<br /> <br /> Cheers all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 07-27-2016, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T10:34:03-07:00","id":938933,"title":"","content":"Oh &quot;Ghost employees&quot; <br /> <br /> What should the opposed roll of the person putting them on the payroll , and guy doing an audit be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:42:57-07:00","id":939096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932599-battles-of-influence-newspapers-police-investigations-etc?p=938933#post938933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh &amp;quot;Ghost employees&amp;quot; <br /> <br /> What should the opposed roll of the person putting them on the payroll , and guy doing an audit be?</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't, it's an audit. Unless your completely forging an entire payroll system to hide something it's going to come out. <br /> <br /> However let's see what attributes one might roll if they were trying to &quot;manipulate&quot; a payroll system in an &quot;intelligent&quot; way to &quot;subterfuge&quot; the fact that the books are cooked.<br /> <br /> The auditor would need to &quot;perceive&quot; in an &quot;intelligent&quot; fashion what he is &quot;investigating&quot; to catch the mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T14:45:40-07:00","id":939152,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your advise Dwight.<br /> <br /> In case anyone didnt know (I didnt until I was well into my twentys) &quot;Ghost Employees&quot; Are employees on the payroll who do not show up for work. either real people who may or may not be in on the fraud (Likely recieving a cut) <br /> <br /> or totally fictious people created for purposes of the fraud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}